      "result_description": "Wadebridge CC - 1st XI - Won",
      "result_applied_to": "36578",
      "match_notes": "Wadebridge maintained their lead at top of County 1 as they ended Newquay's winning run at the Sports Centre. Adam Cocking (26) led the hosts to 51-1 before Cal Morse (2-31) took two in two,and veteran Dave Dunnett produced a sterling spell of 10-5-17-5, including the scalp of the fluent Tom Eggins (36). Connor Pearce (22) got Newquay to 145 with a last wicket of stand of 26, but James Maycock (25) soon erased that to give Wadebridge a flying start. Jon Hancock kept Newquay in it with a an excellent spell of 4-24 as the Bridgers slumped to 92-5, but Ross McLachlan (33*) joined Morse (46*) to ease the visitors home with an unbroken stand of 56. Wadebridge (19pts) were docked a point for a slow over rate, but beat Newquay (5pts) by 5 wickets. ",
